## Water
component-water = Water
component-water-solid-name = Ice
component-water-description-novice = Pure water without impurities. At normal pressure it freezes at 0 °C and boils at 100 °C.
component-water-description-school = It has a very high specific heat (≈ 4200 J/(kg·°C)), so it warms up and cools down slowly. Melting 1 kg of ice takes 334 kJ, boiling away 1 kg of water 2256 kJ.
